# Spec-Driven Development

`AGENTS.md` at the repo root is the canonical contract — workflow (§2), verification (§4),
token discipline (§5), security (§6), git (§7). Cursor reads it natively; follow it.
This rule repeats nothing from it so the two cannot drift.

Cursor-specific:

- Spec Kit is installed as skills under `.cursor/skills/speckit-<name>/`: run
  `speckit-specify`, `speckit-plan`, … `speckit-implement`, then `speckit-converge`.
  The bug lane (`speckit-bug-*`) is installed for Claude Code only; follow
  `.claude/skills/speckit-bug-assess/SKILL.md` by hand, or run
  `specify extension add bug` with Cursor as the active integration.
- Done = `./scripts/verify.sh --full` passed and you read its output. Claude Code's hooks
  may not run under Cursor; CI runs the same script on every push.
